{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ps4 Verified -1 triaged as a KNOWN FLAKE, unrelated to this change. Rechecked with the\nevidence below posted on 1655. LLM-Review+1 holds on ps4.\n\nFAILURE: tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py::test_code_review_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union\n— two clones racing `git push origin HEAD:tickets`, exit 1, xdist worker gw0, CI run\n31628153181.\n\nWHY IT IS NOT THIS CHANGE — four independent lines, checked rather than pattern-matched\n(this change has had four DISTINCT legitimate CI causes, so \"probably the same as last\ntime\" was not an acceptable answer):\n\n1. Named prior art. Bug willing-cellular-carp (1647-19b3-cbec-4a17), \"De-flake sidecar\n   two-clone union fixture sync race\", covers this exact test family — split from\n   chewed-illicit-blacklemur (b8f7-65be-ec00-4844), which was discovered while landing\n   change 1640 and cost THAT change a spurious Verified -1. 1640 is this ticket's sibling\n   from the same stinkpot discovery batch.\n2. Zero linkage. All 9 changed files are the reconciler outbound link path plus a\n   complexity-baseline entry and reconciler unit tests. The failing test drives\n   rebar.llm.code_review.sidecar and tickets-branch pushes; sidecar imports NONE of the\n   changed modules (verified by grep, not assumed).\n3. Lane shape. 1 of 5 lanes failed. The unit lane passed entirely (12320 passed, 66\n   skipped). A real defect in this change failed EVERY lane on ps1 and ps2 — that is the\n   established signature of a deterministic failure here, and this is not it.\n4. Not reproducible. Passes standalone locally, and the whole file passes 3/3 under CI's\n   exact parallel settings (-n 4 --dist loadgroup).\n\nPlausible independent source: the base it ran on, cc69cc1179 \"Retry the write lock instead\nof losing writes\", changes tickets-store write-lock retry — precisely the subsystem this\ntest stresses.\n\nDISCOVERED FINDING WORTH CARRYING. The de-flake commit 78257ce2ff (willing-cellular-carp,\nCLOSED) is ALREADY an ancestor of ps4, so the flake RECURRED despite its fix. That fix\ntargeted the two-clone \"base precondition\" sync race; this manifestation is a failing\n`git push origin HEAD:tickets`, which looks like a different race in the same fixture. So\nwilling-cellular-carp's remedy appears INCOMPLETE rather than wrong. I am not expanding this\nticket's scope to chase it — flagging it for the coordinator to decide whether to reopen\nwilling-cellular-carp or file a sibling, with this run (31628153181) as the fresh evidence."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786562911617218001,"uuid":"6e45133e-263e-4196-b370-68e11245d1d5"}